 "_about": "Shared pronunciation lexicon for every channel's Kokoro voice (owner, 5 Nov 2026: one way to say each tech term). words: the word as written in the script -> Kokoro markup [word](/phonemes/) (misaki US set: A=ay, I=eye, O=oh, W=ow). scripts/voice/say.py swaps the match for that markup (bracket text = the written word without punctuation, so captions still line up). Every reading was checked with Kokoro's own phonemizer (misaki G2P, 5 Nov 2026): the respelling below reads as intended; WiFi, Siri, px, vh, dvh, fps, flexbox, npm, popup, Eiffel and the British spellings are unknown to it and would otherwise go to the espeak fallback. Years (1100-1999, 2010-2099) are said like people say them ('eighteen eighty nine', 'nineteen oh eight'): Kokoro alone reads 1889 as 'eighteen hundred eighty nine'.",
